## Why some of these choices

- **Container filter (`begins with image-uploads`)** stops the audit function from
  triggering on files the process function writes into `image-results`. Without it you can
  get an event loop.
- **SAS token upload** lets the browser upload straight to Blob Storage without exposing the
  account key, and without sending the file through the function.
- **Two storage accounts** (one for my data, one auto-created for the Function App) is normal.
  The Function App needs its own storage for its internal runtime state.

